A person Neutral Citation No. ( 2024:HHC:7119 ) abets the doing of a thing when (1) he instigates any person to do that thing; or (2)
engages with one or more other persons in any conspiracy for the doing of that thing;
or (3) intentionally aids, by act or illegal .

The ingredients of Section 306 IPC have been extensively laid out in M. Arjunan Vs. State, represented by its Inspector of Police7 which are as under: -
"The essential ingredients of the offence under Section 306 I.P.C. are (i) the abetment;
(ii) the intention of the accused to aid or instigate or abet the deceased to commit suicide.
